course: dictionary
lesson: 2122
title: The word converter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A converter is a thing that changes something into something else. The words around it give you clues. «A catalytic converter changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones.» The word changes tells you a converter does not just hold something. It turns it into a different form.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in "a catalytic part changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones". It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Converter can also mean a tool or chart. A unit converter changes inches into centimetres, or pounds into kilograms. The words inches and centimetres are the clue: both are measures, and the converter changes one measure into the other.
fact: A converter is a machine, device or tool that changes something from one form into another.
fact: A unit converter changes amounts from one unit into another, such as inches into centimetres.
fact: A catalytic converter is a part of a car's exhaust that makes the gases less poisonous.
fact: Platinum is rarer than gold and is used in «catalytic converters that clean exhaust fumes».
exercise: «A catalytic converter changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones.» What does a converter do? | Makes cars go faster | Stores water for later | *Changes something into another form | Prints documents
exercise: Which of these is a unit converter? | *An app that changes inches into centimetres | A window blind | A song that plays on a phone | A dog's lead
exercise: «Platinum is rarer than gold and is used in car parts called catalytic converters that clean exhaust fumes.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the converter cleans. | *fumes | carry | rarer | platinum
test: Plug converters are used for travel abroad. What is a plug converter for? | Cleaning sockets | *Letting a plug fit and work in another country | Making plugs louder | Storing batteries
test: In a solar panel, light energy is changed into what? | Sound energy | *Electrical energy | Heat from a fire | Water
exam: «Burnt gases leave through the exhaust pipe, and a catalytic converter changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones.» What does the converter change the gases into? | More poisonous gases | Solid metal dust | Sunlight | *Less harmful gases
